# Redis cache (optional)

Full detail: `docs/architecture/integrations.md`,
`docs/architecture/transactions-and-consistency.md`.

- Enabled only when `REDIS_URL` is set; otherwise a no-op implementation of the same interface.
  Call sites never branch on whether Redis is configured.
- Key `flags:{project_id}:{env}` → JSON `CompiledEnvSnapshot` with `schema_version`; TTL 60s.
  Version mismatch = miss.
- Fail fast: `enableOfflineQueue: false`, `maxRetriesPerRequest: 0`, connect 500ms, command 50ms.
  Circuit opens after 3 consecutive failures for 5s.
- Any Redis error on read → log `warn` (rate-limited), count `result="error"`, load from
  Postgres. Evaluate must never fail because of Redis (NFR-REL-001).
- Singleflight concurrent misses per key (FR-CACHE-003).
- Only the read path writes to the cache. Admin mutations only delete keys, after commit.
- Every new cache key needs a matching invalidation path and an integration test proving a
  mutation is visible to evaluate immediately after the 2xx.
